From: village <village@flint3-port>
Subject: hsl: hsl_phy: drop removed phy_device.eee_enabled field write

phy_device.eee_enabled was removed upstream; EEE state is now tracked via
phy_device.eee_active (private, managed by phylib itself) and the
linkmode-based advertising_eee bitmask this same function already sets
correctly via linkmode_mod_bit() immediately below. The removed line was
a plain boolean mirror of what the linkmode bits already express, not
additional information -- safe to drop rather than map to a new field.

--- a/src/hsl/phy/hsl_phy.c
+++ b/src/hsl/phy/hsl_phy.c
@@ -1881,8 +1881,6 @@
 	rv = hsl_phy_phydev_get(dev_id, phy_addr, &phydev);
 	SW_RTN_ON_ERROR(rv);

-	phydev->eee_enabled = (adv == 0 ? A_FALSE : A_TRUE);
-
 	linkmode_mod_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_100baseT_Full_BIT,
 		phydev->advertising_eee, adv & FAL_PHY_EEE_100BASE_T);
 	linkmode_mod_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_1000baseT_Full_BIT,
